'''Iakaru''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Iakar]]. [[Bistan]] was a member of this species.

==Biology and appearance==
Having evolved in a [[jungle]] canopy, Iakaru had exceptional spatial awareness, aided by sensitive brow tufts. Swinging through the dense [[tree]]s required keen [[eye]]sight, accurate depth perception, and quick reflexes.<ref name="Visual Guide" />

==History==
[[File:Iakaru_Victorious_DoR.png|thumb|left|200px|An Iakaru stands over a fallen [[death trooper]].]]
Many Iakaru were [[Massacres on Iakar|massacred]] during the [[Clone Wars]] by corporate powers.<ref name="Dawn">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]''</ref> At the [[time]] of the [[Battle of Scarif]], Iakaru were an uncommon sight in [[the galaxy]], as they had not developed [[hyperdrive]] technology. Their [[homeworld]] [[Iakar]] had been visited by interstellar trade for nearly a [[Standard century|century]]. Pharmaceutical corporations drew valuable organic compounds from the lush rain [[forest]]s girdling the [[planet]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], companies set up major research installations on Iakar, which drove the Iakaru deeper into the jungle and strained the tentative trading relationships the natives had established with the offworlders. With the [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] and its [[Imperial Military|military]] expansion, demand for medical supplies escalated, which brought a full-scale Imperial seizure and [[occupation of Iakar]].<ref name="Visual Guide" />

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Iakaru were created for [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|anthology]] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''. Concept art of them was done by [[Ivan Manzella]] and [[Adam Brockbank]].<ref name="ArtofRO">''[[The Art of Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> [[Pablo Hidalgo]] named the Iakaru after the [[Wikipedia:Amazon rainforest|Amazonian]] [[Wikipedia:Uakari|uakari]] [[Wikipedia:Monkey|monkey]].<ref name="Much to Learn">{{SW|url=news/much-to-learn-you-still-have-talking-rogue-one-aliens-with-pablo-hidalgo|text=Much to Learn You Still Have: Talking ''Rogue One'' Aliens with Pablo Hidalgo}}</ref> They first appeared prior to the release of the film, in the [[Star Wars video games|mobile video game]] ''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]'' on November 1, 2016.<ref name="GoH forums">{{EA|subdomain=forums.galaxy-of-heroes.starwars|url=discussion/74049/game-update-10-27-2016|text=Game Update - 10/27/2016|archivedate=20170225204713|nolive=1}}</ref>

